    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d229">

                <pb facs="0721" n="688" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76v12/pg688"/>

                <head>229. Transcript of Telephone Conversation Between the President’s Assistant
                    for National Security Affairs (Kissinger) and the Soviet Ambassador
                        (Dobrynin)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d229-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1970-10-09T22:20:00-04:00">October 9, 1970, 10:20 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline></opener>
                <p> D: You are not still in bed?</p>
                <p> K: No.</p>
                <p> D: Oh good, you see I would like to clarify some points beginning on the Cuba
                        paper<anchor n="2" xml:id="d229-f2"/> you gave me dealing with nuclear and
                    atomic things. One is the construction of submarines or surface repair
                    facilities ashore in Cuba. You do not use any reference to nuclear or atomic in
                    points covering this issue in the note. It refers in the heading to strategic
                    systems, is that what is meant concerning repair facilities?</p>
                <p> K: We are talking about ships in the above mentioned categories. (i.e. nuclear
                    and atomic)</p>
                <p> D: Just would like to be sure, they will ask me. I was under the impression that
                    this was so but I wanted to be sure.</p>
                <p> K: Yes, that’s correct.</p>
                <p> D: This is important. Thank you. Have a nice weekend.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
